<title>SWEDEN: Swedish mobile phone sales rise sharply in March.</title>
<headline>Swedish mobile phone sales rise sharply in March.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of mobile telephones sold in Sweden rose sharply in March to 133,317 compared to 58,098 in March last year, industry group Mobile Telephone Deliverers said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Of the total number sold last month, 130,529 were GSM (Global System for Mobile Communications) phones.</p>
<p>Over the past 12 months, a total of 1.17 million mobile phones have been sold in Sweden, an increase of 39.4 percent from the previous 12 month period.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
